  "description": "Discontinued. This page is kept as an archive record for owners and for anyone researching an older Cotic BFe. The information on this page is for historical reference.\n\nYears of production: 2005-2016\n\nThe classic BFe 26 was later replaced by a new BFe 26 with updated geometry: see BFe 26 (2018). The BFe 26's brother was the BFe 275: see the BFe archive.\n\nThe BFe 26 is the hardnut of the Cotic family. It shares its geometry with our Soul 26 frame (see the Soul archive), but the BFe 26 likes a more, shall we say, direct approach.\n\nThe BFe 26 is for hard riding. You can run with a 100mm fork for 4X and dirtjump duties. You can plug in a 160mm fork and send it, but don't oversend it, down the Megavalanche. Those are the two extremes of the fork build options. Most BFe 26 builds end up somewhere in between and perform mighty fine as bold-as-brass rag-around play bikes.\n\nFun with a capital F, Durable with a capital D: Burly Iron.",
